  "timeframe": "Last 14 days up to 2026-11-25T16:38:17Z",
  "criteria": "Report concisely: (1) Which AWS/Bedrock metrics exist (Invocations, InvocationLatency, InvocationClientErrors/ServerErrors, InvocationThrottles, TimeToFirstToken, token counts, etc.), which models/modelIds, how far back data goes, any gaps; and a quick read of InvocationLatency trend (p50/p90/p99 or avg) per model over the 14 days showing when it worsened, if it did. (2) Whether model invocation logging is enabled (get_model_invocation_logging_configuration), its destinations (CloudWatch Logs / S3), and whether text/embedding data delivery is on, and whether logs actually contain recent records. (3) Whether callers (Lambda/ECS/EKS apps) emit traces (X-Ray/OTel) or app logs/metrics around Bedrock calls, and which workloads call Bedrock if discoverable. (4) Whether CloudTrail/config history can show changes (e.g., model/provisioned throughput changes, guardrails, inference profile/cross-region config, quota changes) and Service Quotas visibility for Bedrock throttling. (5) Alarms on Bedrock metrics. Finish with a clear verdict: sufficient / partial / insufficient telemetry, listing specific gaps and what to enable to close them. Read-only operations only."
